! Regressions found running the "Designing Optics Using CODE V" examples
! a missing lens file is reported, and FIR without a lens refuses (crashed)
RES nosuchlens
FIR
! THI SI (image defocus): paraxial slopes, THO, FNO and exit pupil stay
! finite, and the exit pupil does not move with the defocus (was NaN)
LEN NEW
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -32.4637
PIM
FIR
THI SI -1
PXTY ALL
THO
FIR
THI SI 0
! FLY keeps the image solve and the paraxial trace follows the flipped lens:
! PIM 47.3762, SA -0.40526 (book Table 6.3; was the unflipped lens)
FLY S1..2
SUR SA
THO
! SCA rescales what the paraxial trace sees: EFL lands on 50 exactly
LEN NEW
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -50
PIM
SCA EFL 50
FIR
! TOW headless runs its commands with ordinary output (segfaulted)
TOW
FIR
GO
! an unknown glass is refused; the surface keeps its glass (was n=1.0)
GLA S1 GERMLW_SPECIAL
SUR SA
! WL without REF: the reference is the center wavelength (book eye model,
! Table 4.5: EFL 22.1078 / 16.5845 in air)
LEN NEW
WL 656.27 587.56 486.13
EPD 6
YAN 0 14 25
INS S1..2
STOP S2
RDY S1 7.8
THI S1 3.6
GLA S1 WATER
RDY S2 10
THI S2 3.6
GLA S2 1.415:47.0
RDY S3 -6
GLA S3 WATER
RDY S4 -10
PIM
FIR
! working F-number at finite conjugates from the real object angle (book
! Table 3.2: FNO 7.4108 at 125 mm)
LEN NEW
EPD 20
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -50
PIM
THI SO 125
FIR
! a concave mirror has a positive EFL (book: EFL = -R/2)
LEN NEW
EPD 20
RDY S1 -100
RMD S1 REFL
PIM
FIR
! THO in CODE V's columns, colour F-C (book Table 9.3: AX -0.020445
! -0.017544, LAT -0.005310 0.004822 at the default field)
LEN NEW
WL 656.2725 587.5618 486.1327
EPD 5
INS S2
RDY S1 32.46367
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -120
PIM
THO
